**Test filters.** For this step these gates run only the tests their filter selects (plus any inherited expected-red tests); put the tests this step adds or changes where a filter value finds them:
- `constructor-unit-tests`: 
- `ui-smoke`: 
- `ui-tests`: `OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.DataFilePickerFolderTests`, `OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.InverseConstructorTests`, `OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.ScrollExtentTests`, `OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.SolverHandoffWindowTests`

**How to implement.** An experiment's data file becomes a kit attachment, read through the kit by its relative path (001 §E 'References inside a kit are relative paths …', 'Absolute paths are never stored'; the S4.2 brief: `Experiments.DataFilePath`, an absolute path string today, is replaced by `DataAttachment` in `Experiment.dataFileOpt` and `attachDataFile`; `ExperimentDataStore.createFileBacked` and `ExperimentDataLoad.loadAndValidate` read through the kit by relative path; no kit file stores an absolute path). This is one step because the record field's type changes every consumer at once. (1) Domain. (a) `OpticalConstructor.Domain/Experiments.fs` opens `Kit`. `DataFilePath` (`Experiments.fs:DataFilePath`) is deleted. `Experiment.dataFileOpt` (`Experiments.fs:Experiment`) becomes `DataAttachment option` (step 132), and `attachDataFile` (`Experiments.fs:attachDataFile`) takes `(attachment : DataAttachment)`. Their docs say the attachment is a kit-relative path and its hash (spec 0050 S4.2). (b) `OpticalConstructor.Domain/MeasuredData.fs`, after `DataFileText` (`MeasuredData.fs:DataFileText`): `type Kit.KitFileText with member this.dataFileText : DataFileText` hands a kit file's text to the measured-data parsers, in one direction only (ELEV006). Its doc is one line. (c) `OpticalConstructor.Domain/ExperimentDataProxy.fs`: `ExperimentDataProxy` (`ExperimentDataProxy.fs:ExperimentDataProxy`) opens `Kit` and becomes `{ attachDataFile : FileName -> Result<DataAttachment, KitError>; attachmentStatus : DataAttachment -> Result<DataAttachmentStatus, KitError>; tryLoadIntensity : DataAttachment -> Result<IntensitySeries, ExperimentDataError>; tryLoadEllipsometric : DataAttachment -> Result<EllipsometricSeries, ExperimentDataError> }`, still `[<ReferenceEquality>]`. Each field has a one-line doc: attach a picked file to the kit, in place inside it and copied into `data/` otherwise; the attachment's status now; and the two loads by the attachment's kit path. The module and record docs say, in one to three lines each, that the seam reads through one kit (spec 0050 S4.2). Their paragraphs about the DECLARED lifecycle and a future file adapter are deleted, because that lifecycle ended at spec 0038 step 36. (d) `OpticalConstructor.Domain/ExperimentDataLoad.fs`: the last parameter of `loadAndValidate` (`ExperimentDataLoad.fs:loadAndValidate`) becomes `(attachment : DataAttachment)`, passed to the loads. Nothing else changes. (e) The docs of `ExperimentCollectionStore.fs` that name `DataFilePath` say `DataAttachment`. (2) Storage. In `OpticalConstructor.Storage/ExperimentDataStore.fs`, `createFileBacked ()` (`ExperimentDataStore.fs:createFileBacked`) becomes `createFileBacked (kit : KitProxy) : ExperimentDataProxy`. `attachDataFile file` reads the picked file into a `FileByteContent` where the bytes are read (`File.ReadAllBytes`; any exception is caught there and answered `KitIoErr` naming the file and the exception's message), then answers `kit.attachLabFile KitDataFolder.root` of `{ file = file; content = <that content> }` (step 134). `attachmentStatus` is `kit.attachmentStatus` (step 134). `loadThrough` (`ExperimentDataStore.fs:loadThrough`) reads `kit.readDataFile attachment.path` (step 128). A `KitError` is `MalformedDataFileErr` with today's text form, `could not read the <kind> data file '<kit path>': <describe>`, staying within the four-case channel, and the file's `text.dataFileText` goes to the parser unchanged. The module doc says, in one to three lines, that the seam reads through the kit it is built over and that the picked file's read is its one IO of its own. (3) Ui. (a) `OpticalConstructor.Ui/AppContext.fs`, where `AppContext` composes `experimentData` (`AppContext.fs:AppContext.create`; `compose` since step 89), and `TableAndElementRotationView.fs`'s `defaultExperimentProxies`: `experimentData` is `ExperimentDataStore.createFileBacked (KitProxy.createInMemory (InMemoryKitFolder.create ()))`, the session's in-memory kit, as the scene and collection seams beside it are in-memory stores. The `experimentData` field doc says so in one line. (b) `OpticalConstructor.Ui/ConstructorUiIdOfDomain.fs`: `type KitError with member this.caption : ControlCaption` is its `describe` (step 122), with a one-line doc, beside the other error captions. (c) `OpticalConstructor.Ui/TableAndElementRotationView.fs`. `ExperimentFileStatus` (`TableAndElementRotationView.fs:ExperimentFileStatus`) gains `DataFileAttachFailed of reason : ControlCaption`, captioned `Attach failed — <reason>`. `AttachDataFileTo` (`TableAndElementRotationView.fs:TableAndElementRotationMsg`) carries `Experiments.ExperimentId * FileName`, the picked file, and its doc says the kit records it. Its update arm calls `model.experimentData.attachDataFile`. On `Error e` the experiment keeps what it had, and its status is `DataFileAttachFailed e.caption`. On `Ok attachment` it is today's arm over `attachDataFile experimentId attachment` and `loadAndValidate … attachment`. `pickDataFile` (`TableAndElementRotationView.fs:pickDataFile`) passes `FileName file.Path.LocalPath`, and its `onPicked` takes a `FileName`. `dataFileRow` shows `file: <the attachment's kit path>`. Every comment that names `DataFilePath` names the attachment or the picked file. (d) `OpticalConstructor.Ui/UserEnvironment.fs`: the `type Experiments.DataFilePath with` extension (`UserEnvironment.fs:443-447`) is deleted, because `FileName.tryGetFolderName` (STL `Sys/Primitives.fs`) gives the same answer. `rememberFolder`'s `selectedFile` and `DataFilePick.FilePicked` (`UserEnvironment.fs:rememberFolder`, `UserEnvironment.fs:DataFilePick`) take a `FileName`. (e) `OpticalConstructor.Ui/SolverHandoffView.fs`: `handoffFileCaption` shows the attachment's kit path, and `validateExperiment` (`SolverHandoffView.fs:validateExperiment`) passes the attachment to `loadAndValidate`. The doc of `SolverHandoffWindow.fs` names the measured-data seam over the kit where it names the step-36 load seam. (4) The project-file comments that name `DataFilePath`, in `OpticalConstructor.Domain.fsproj` and `OpticalConstructor.Tests.fsproj`, name the data attachment in no more words. Nothing is added. (5) Tests. Each fixture attachment is born as a `DataAttachment` with a `data/…` path and a test-local 64-character lowercase hex hash literal. `ExperimentDataProxyTests`: the mock is keyed by the attachment's path, answers `attachDataFile` with an attachment at `data/<leaf>` and `attachmentStatus` with `AttachedDataUnchanged`. `a mock ExperimentDataProxy loads canned intensity and ellipsometric series through their exact signatures` and `an unknown path yields a typed ExperimentDataError from both fields, never a throw` keep their assertions over attachments at `data/run-intensity.csv`, `data/run-ellipsometric.csv` and `data/nowhere.csv`. `ExperimentDataStoreTests` builds each proxy as `createFileBacked (KitProxy.create (KitFolder (FolderName <a new GUID folder under the class's testDir>)))` and places each fixture text at `data/<name>` itself, its attachment being `readDataFile`'s. Its four facts keep their names and assertions, the missing-file one over an attachment whose path holds no file. It gains `createFileBacked copies a picked file from outside the kit into data and records one inside the kit in place`: a picked file the test wrote outside the kit folder attaches as `data/<its name>` holding its bytes, and a picked file the test wrote inside the kit's `data` folder attaches in place, writing nothing; and `createFileBacked answers KitIoErr for a picked file it cannot read and attaches nothing`: a picked name that does not exist answers `KitIoErr` naming it, and the kit holds nothing new. `ExperimentProxyTests`: `DataFilePath elevates a raw path and attachDataFile binds one per experiment` becomes `attachDataFile binds one data attachment per experiment`, over an attachment at `data/run1.csv`. `ExperimentCollectionProxyTests`' `a stub ExperimentCollectionProxy over a fixed map exercises saveCollection, tryLoadCollection, and listCollections through their exact signatures` and `ExperimentCollectionRoundTripTests`' `createInMemory round-trips a collection of E1 (full) / E2 (sample-less) / E3 (dark), preserving ordered setups, optional shapes, and DataFilePath attachments`, renamed `createInMemory round-trips a collection of E1 (full) / E2 (sample-less) / E3 (dark), preserving ordered setups, optional shapes, and data attachments`, carry attachments at `data/run1.csv`, `data/e1-transmitted.csv` and `data/e3-dark.csv`, and keep their assertions. `InverseConstructorTests`: `mockIntensity` and `mockEllipsometric` answer `attachDataFile` with `data/<the picked file's leaf>` and `attachmentStatus` with `AttachedDataUnchanged`. The facts dispatch `AttachDataFileTo` with a `FileName` and assert the attachment's path, `data/measured.csv` and `data/run.csv`, keeping every other assertion: `attaching a valid intensity file records a typed Loaded status and the attachment`, `attaching a malformed intensity file records a typed parse-error status`, `attaching an out-of-range intensity file records a typed validation-error status`, `the detector kind selects the ellipsometric load path`, `a named collection round-trips through save, list, and load` and the `ui-smoke` fact `the inverse workbench renders the collection builder without throwing`. It gains `a picked file the kit cannot attach records a typed attach-failed status and no attachment`: over a mock whose `attachDataFile` answers `KitIoErr`, `AttachDataFileTo` leaves the experiment's `dataFileOpt` `None` and its status `DataFileAttachFailed`, whose caption holds the reason. `DataFilePickerFolderTests`' five facts that pick a file (`a confirmed selection records the file's folder under the purpose key`, `a cancel leaves the persisted folder untouched`, `the next open passes the persisted folder as the picker start folder`, `a re-pick in a new folder replaces the persisted folder`, `a bare filename with no directory part leaves the folder map untouched`) pick a `FileName` and keep their assertions. `SolverHandoffWindowTests`' `withFile` attaches `data/<name>`, and its mocks gain the two fields and are keyed by the attachment's path; `ScrollExtentTests`' `noData` gains the two fields. Every fact of both keeps its assertions. After this step, `git grep -n -w DataFilePath -- Berreman/OpticalConstructor ":(exclude)*/MuellerReconstruction.fs" ":(exclude)*/MuellerDataStore.fs"` finds nothing. The two excluded files keep spec 0044's history note, because they belong to S9's removals.

**Acceptance.** After the switch, `Experiment.dataFileOpt` MUST hold a `DataAttachment`, `ExperimentDataStore.createFileBacked` MUST read and attach through the kit it is built over, and `git grep -n -w DataFilePath -- Berreman/OpticalConstructor ":(exclude)*/MuellerReconstruction.fs" ":(exclude)*/MuellerDataStore.fs"` MUST find nothing; constructor-unit-tests MUST pass, including `createFileBacked copies a picked file from outside the kit into data and records one inside the kit in place`, `createFileBacked answers KitIoErr for a picked file it cannot read and attaches nothing`, the renamed `attachDataFile binds one data attachment per experiment` and `createInMemory round-trips a collection of E1 (full) / E2 (sample-less) / E3 (dark), preserving ordered setups, optional shapes, and data attachments`, the count rising by 2; ui-smoke MUST pass, including `the inverse workbench renders the collection builder without throwing`; ui-tests MUST pass over the selected classes, including `a picked file the kit cannot attach records a typed attach-failed status and no attachment`, the count rising by 1; and build, elevation and the eleven s16 invariants MUST pass.
